Create a new placement group.

USAGE:
  scw instance placement-group create [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Create a max availability placement group with default name
    scw instance placement-group create

  Create a max availability placement group with the specified name
    scw instance placement-group create name=foobar

  Create a low latency placement group
    scw instance placement-group create policy-type=low_latency

  Create a max availability placement group with tags
    scw instance placement-group create tags.0=foo tags.1=bar

ARGS:
  [project-id]                     Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [name=<generated>]               Name of the placement group
  [policy-type=max_availability]   Policy type of the placement group (unknown_policy_type | low_latency | max_availability)
  [tags.{index}]                   Tags of the placement group
  [zone=fr-par-1]                  Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for create
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
